#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dd6988a-86b8-5b56-bf3e-fc0df20e099b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities With Variables on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "9f887f78-3ba8-540d-af89-1c3166ee6c38" :question/math-academy-id "e-12970" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $5x+13 \\ge 3x-7$ and sketch the solution on the number line." :question/worked-solution "We solve the inequality just like we would solve an equation.\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+13 & \\ge 3x-7 \\\\ 5x+13-3x & \\ge 3x-7-3x \\\\ 2x+13 & \\ge -7 \\\\ 2x+13-13 & \\ge -7-13 \\\\ 2x & \\ge -20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the multiplication principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & \\ge -20 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\ge \\frac{-20}{2} \\\\ x & \\ge -10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x \\ge -10.$\n\nOur solution can be expressed using a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/04/04b9a164fbff3b0603dcbd2b3283ad44ba480af91ae9af3dbd4ddcfe086c0752.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215dc4e3-bf30-538d-bc8c-d67d6a60e12b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing a Rational Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "232b1ad9-6651-582b-b942-b36c7896806e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12971" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{2-5y}{3} \\le 4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2-5y}{3} & \\le 4 \\\\ 3\\cdot (\\frac{2-5y}{3}) & \\le 3\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2-5y}{\\cancel{3}}) & \\le 3\\cdot 4 \\\\ 2-5y & \\le 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles. \n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-5y & \\le 12 \\\\ 2-5y-2 & \\le 12-2 \\\\ -5y & \\le 10 \\\\ \\frac{-5y}{-5} & \\,\\,\\ge \\,\\,\\frac{10}{-5} \\\\ y & \\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y \\ge -2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192545 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9374b546-aa83-53f6-b38d-fc750350e659" :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities With Rational Expression and Variables on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "bab434ec-d18a-5d77-9bf1-8e16e9af2556" :question/math-academy-id "e-12974" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4y -1 > \\dfrac {5y - 2} {3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-1 & >\\frac{5y-2}{3} \\\\ 3\\cdot (4y-1) & >3\\cdot (\\frac{5y-2}{3}) \\\\ 3\\cdot (4y-1) & >\\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{5y-2}{\\cancel{3}}) \\\\ 3\\cdot (4y-1) & >5y-2 \\\\ 12y-3 & >5y-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t12y-3\t&> 5y-2 \\[5pt]\n\t\t12y-3-5y\t&> 5y-2-5y \\[5pt]\n\t\t7y-3\t&> {-2} \\[5pt]\n\t\t7y-3 +3\t&> {-2} +3 \\[5pt]\n\t\t7y\t\t&> {1} \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{7y}{7}\t&> \\dfrac{1}7 \\[5pt]\n\t\ty\t\t&> \\dfrac{1}{7}\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y > \\dfrac17.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192546 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a00ac76c-0ebd-53cb-b689-98bda731064a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing Two Rational Expressions"}] :question/id #uuid "8740f864-62be-5391-bf06-ac4f4e1c1a2c" :question/math-academy-id "e-12975" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{3a-2}{5} > \\dfrac{4+6a}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expressions by multiplying both sides of the inequality by the lowest common positive multiple of the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3a-2}{5} & >\\frac{4+6a}{2} \\\\ 10\\cdot (\\frac{3a-2}{5}) & >10\\cdot (\\frac{4+6a}{2}) \\\\ 2\\cdot (3a-2) & >5\\cdot (4+6a) \\\\ 6a-4 & >20+30a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles. \n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-4 & >20+30a \\\\ 6a-4-30a & >20+30a-30a \\\\ -4-24a & >20 \\\\ -4-24a+4 & >20+4 \\\\ -24a & >24 \\\\ \\frac{-24a}{-24} & \\,\\,<\\,\\,\\frac{24}{-24} \\\\ a & <-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a < -1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dd6988a-86b8-5b56-bf3e-fc0df20e099b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities With Variables on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "459c368d-341b-5652-9212-c84e4e6265bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506840} {:answer/id #uuid "51a58d75-f23f-5897-9e00-ccb145f6a7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506865} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0bc2eb-f9f9-5fdb-8a9c-09767152a293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506949} {:answer/id #uuid "98a54cb3-6a54-5ceb-839e-58b2de20f8a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507010} {:answer/id #uuid "9f210a49-d5a0-54be-a949-a3c51522c88c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98a54cb3-6a54-5ceb-839e-58b2de20f8a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507010} :answer-field/id #uuid "e92f18f8-e06f-59d8-b904-14cbf96f836e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f01d823-c35d-5548-8b98-ed400d817eaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-154885" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $3-y>2y+5.$" :question/worked-solution "We solve the inequality just like we would solve an equation.\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-y & >2y+5 \\\\ 3-y-2y & >2y+5-2y \\\\ 3-3y & >5 \\\\ 3-3y-3 & >5-3 \\\\ -3y & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the multiplication principle.\n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y & >2 \\\\ \\frac{-3y}{-3} & \\,\\,<\\,\\,\\frac{2}{-3} \\\\ y & <-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dd6988a-86b8-5b56-bf3e-fc0df20e099b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities With Variables on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19633220-159c-5dfb-bf8b-34b50318a3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506724} {:answer/id #uuid "5b463819-a297-5905-a3c9-e9c8dd05bde6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\le -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506894} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd17978-47c8-5c12-b633-3f58884989e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506931} {:answer/id #uuid "a899db60-6f87-5391-b2f0-c5acd81c5e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507047} {:answer/id #uuid "ea7de015-56c0-5867-aff1-dbc185e93088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\le -\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b463819-a297-5905-a3c9-e9c8dd05bde6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\le -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506894} :answer-field/id #uuid "297f7d05-1897-5a97-a21e-3bb7c98bf25a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dcf98c54-1401-5d68-8eaa-0aa383d87a96" :question/math-academy-id "q-154888" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4u-11\\ge 9u+4.$" :question/worked-solution "We solve the inequality just like we would solve an equation.\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-11 & \\ge 9u+4 \\\\ 4u-11-9u & \\ge 9u+4-9u \\\\ -11-5u & \\ge 4 \\\\ -11-5u+11 & \\ge 4+11 \\\\ -5u & \\ge 15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the multiplication principle.\n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5u & \\ge 15 \\\\ \\frac{-5u}{-5} & \\,\\,\\le \\,\\,\\frac{15}{-5} \\\\ u & \\le -3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a00ac76c-0ebd-53cb-b689-98bda731064a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing Two Rational Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3baa451a-05ef-5ea6-9e67-38333ef4f803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506819} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad18f48-f87f-5a8e-83ca-7b7baaf8d85b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge 14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506892} {:answer/id #uuid "9976ab5e-8eac-58d3-a410-a11083f1fd8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507012} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ea89bc-8d49-5eb8-bdf1-af8685391da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le 14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507027} {:answer/id #uuid "ece206a6-bb4a-5ca0-a27c-6ac1106fcba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9976ab5e-8eac-58d3-a410-a11083f1fd8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507012} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd44771e-0700-538a-9998-e17199c5831d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "37bbccda-0b14-5e04-9a10-40c81c14c83e" :question/math-academy-id "q-156048" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{2y-8}{3}\\le \\frac{8-2y}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expressions by multiplying both sides of the inequality by the lowest common positive multiple of the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y-8}{3} & \\le \\frac{8-2y}{4} \\\\ 12\\cdot (\\frac{2y-8}{3}) & \\le 12\\cdot (\\frac{8-2y}{4}) \\\\ 4\\cdot (2y-8) & \\le 3\\cdot (8-2y) \\\\ 8y-32 & \\le 24-6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8y-32 & \\le 24-6y \\\\ 8y-32+6y & \\le 24-6y+6y \\\\ 14y-32 & \\le 24 \\\\ 14y-32+32 & \\le 24+32 \\\\ 14y & \\le 56 \\\\ \\frac{14y}{14} & \\le \\frac{56}{14} \\\\ y & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y\\le 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a00ac76c-0ebd-53cb-b689-98bda731064a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing Two Rational Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c2fead-d108-57e7-8db0-525fce50e750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506713} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9dca56-0354-57b4-a7e8-d9a0ef2a39c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506778} {:answer/id #uuid "696f454f-a239-53c4-b608-6d6ad371cc2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506925} {:answer/id #uuid "bd5e7ebb-9abc-5d94-9362-95adeacf2f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507095} {:answer/id #uuid "e177af7e-0bf6-5205-9657-9a0ed5250651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11c2fead-d108-57e7-8db0-525fce50e750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506713} :answer-field/id #uuid "78e5e08f-692a-52d5-9828-56a741cd6532" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fd93fd8-c1db-5a78-b0d6-62c128a57e89" :question/math-academy-id "q-156057" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{4y-9}{15}<\\frac{y}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expressions by multiplying both sides of the inequality by the lowest common positive multiple of the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4y-9}{15} & <\\frac{y}{3} \\\\ 15\\cdot (\\frac{4y-9}{15}) & <15\\cdot (\\frac{y}{3}) \\\\ 4y-9 & <5y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles. \n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-9 & <5y \\\\ 4y-9-5y & <5y-5y \\\\ -9-y & <0 \\\\ -9-y+9 & <0+9 \\\\ -y & <9 \\\\ \\frac{-y}{-1} & \\,\\,>\\,\\,\\frac{9}{-1} \\\\ y & >-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y>-9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a00ac76c-0ebd-53cb-b689-98bda731064a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing Two Rational Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1af436a9-9425-59bc-9879-b5a2d4148878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\le 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506726} {:answer/id #uuid "32818b35-b7cb-56f3-b1f3-4d1137800999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\le -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506799} {:answer/id #uuid "63abf159-1bb5-5a42-9daa-463b46621411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\ge 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506915} {:answer/id #uuid "a20e1ecc-b32b-5179-94f5-f6fcfeabd193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\ge -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507028} {:answer/id #uuid "fda207e8-8fff-5625-a4ee-cd07bda49aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a20e1ecc-b32b-5179-94f5-f6fcfeabd193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\ge -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507028} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ad7f7db-4030-5bba-a9d1-a46ba85090e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8e1188e-48d5-534b-bcfd-6a2d0af01921" :question/math-academy-id "q-156062" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{2a-4}{8}\\le \\frac{2a}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expressions by multiplying both sides of the inequality by the lowest common positive multiple of the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2a-4}{8} & \\le \\frac{2a}{6} \\\\ 24\\cdot (\\frac{2a-4}{8}) & \\le 24\\cdot (\\frac{2a}{6}) \\\\ 3\\cdot (2a-4) & \\le 4\\cdot 2a \\\\ 6a-12 & \\le 8a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles. \n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-12 & \\le 8a \\\\ 6a-12-8a & \\le 8a-8a \\\\ -12-2a & \\le 0 \\\\ -12-2a+12 & \\le 0+12 \\\\ -2a & \\le 12 \\\\ \\frac{-2a}{-2} & \\,\\,\\ge \\,\\,\\frac{12}{-2} \\\\ a & \\ge -6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a\\ge -6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215dc4e3-bf30-538d-bc8c-d67d6a60e12b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing a Rational Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e90f66c1-50aa-5eec-9fca-bddb4bba7214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e90f66c1-50aa-5eec-9fca-bddb4bba7214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507194} :answer-field/id #uuid "41f396f4-a600-561c-a811-891b140e8ab6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5197d664-2d80-5cab-8f1a-7a61713e0053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5197d664-2d80-5cab-8f1a-7a61713e0053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506864} :answer-field/id #uuid "835c17f7-36ef-548e-8b46-b6d83fc2e63a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf4150db-c6d9-5a42-a567-768a11a0a924" :question/math-academy-id "q-171616" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $\\frac{5z+2}{3}\\ge 4.$\n\n$z$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5z+2}{3} & \\ge 4 \\\\ 3\\cdot (\\frac{5z+2}{3}) & \\ge 3\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{5z+2}{\\cancel{3}}) & \\ge 12 \\\\ 5z+2 & \\ge 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5z+2 & \\ge 12 \\\\ 5z+2-2 & \\ge 12-2 \\\\ 5z & \\ge 10 \\\\ \\frac{5z}{5} & \\ge \\frac{10}{5} \\\\ z & \\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z\\ge 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507456 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215dc4e3-bf30-538d-bc8c-d67d6a60e12b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing a Rational Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "686fb959-8e23-5381-8bd9-2f970d41778e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "686fb959-8e23-5381-8bd9-2f970d41778e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506922} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fbfa6a5-6a10-5832-a94e-61877fd05794" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507328} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f5f8125-cec1-5372-9fa6-f054c0ec30d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f5f8125-cec1-5372-9fa6-f054c0ec30d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507020} :answer-field/id #uuid "b06e3cb5-1f20-5499-8cd9-ff51fcfab7bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88277403-5532-598b-ac5e-1cdba1716886" :question/math-academy-id "q-181353" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $\\frac{5t-6}{2}\\le 1.$\n\nThe solution is $t$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5t-6}{2}\\le 1 \\\\ 2\\cdot (\\frac{5t-6}{2}) & \\le 2\\cdot 1 \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot (\\frac{5t-6}{\\cancel{2}}) & \\le 2 \\\\ 5t-6 & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5t-6 & \\le 2 \\\\ 5t-6+6 & \\le 2+6 \\\\ 5t & \\le 8 \\\\ \\frac{5t}{5} & \\le \\frac{8}{5} \\\\ t & \\le \\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t\\le \\frac{8}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215dc4e3-bf30-538d-bc8c-d67d6a60e12b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing a Rational Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9b0d25f-a9be-59cb-9e73-c90c91605ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9b0d25f-a9be-59cb-9e73-c90c91605ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507052} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f3c02df-5522-58ab-abd4-e9b78610a514" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdcb9fbd-5555-5112-b178-4b472e36dad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdcb9fbd-5555-5112-b178-4b472e36dad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507126} :answer-field/id #uuid "719477eb-00fb-512e-85cd-7a35def7de91" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41e3b8c9-bf8c-5f28-a82e-0ab2c9c99da3" :question/math-academy-id "q-181364" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $\\frac{1-7x}{5}\\ge 2.$\n\nThe solution is $x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-7x}{5} & \\ge 2 \\\\ 5\\cdot (\\frac{1-7x}{5}) & \\ge 5\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\cancel{5}\\cdot (\\frac{1-7x}{\\cancel{5}}) & \\ge 10 \\\\ 1-7x & \\ge 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles.\n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-7x & \\ge 10 \\\\ 1-7x-1 & \\ge 10-1 \\\\ -7x & \\ge 9 \\\\ \\frac{-7x}{-7} & \\,\\,\\le \\,\\,\\frac{9}{-7} \\\\ x & \\le -\\frac{9}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le -\\frac{9}{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9374b546-aa83-53f6-b38d-fc750350e659" :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities With Rational Expression and Variables on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b4e37a9-9371-541d-b046-02330a84b683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b4e37a9-9371-541d-b046-02330a84b683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507015} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6100537-9c91-5945-8d50-4bf692d695a1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507346} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "656c88fd-0784-5c15-95e4-e68ff8d0009a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "656c88fd-0784-5c15-95e4-e68ff8d0009a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506918} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae484b73-c158-5737-8b58-c8813ea0f8cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a763aa0a-1786-546d-877a-3f8cb8ed771a" :question/math-academy-id "q-181373" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $\\frac{2-3p}{4}<2p+1.$\n\nThe solution is $p$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2-3p}{4} & <2p+1 \\\\ 4\\cdot (\\frac{2-3p}{4}) & <4\\cdot (2p+1) \\\\ \\cancel{4}\\cdot (\\frac{2-3p}{\\cancel{4}}) & <4\\cdot (2p+1) \\\\ 2-3p & <8p+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles. \n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-3p & <8p+4 \\\\ 2-3p-8p & <8p+4-8p \\\\ 2-11p & <4 \\\\ 2-11p-2 & <4-2 \\\\ -11p & <2 \\\\ \\frac{-11p}{-11} & \\,\\,>\\,\\,\\frac{2}{-11} \\\\ p & >-\\frac{2}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p>-\\frac{2}{11}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9374b546-aa83-53f6-b38d-fc750350e659" :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities With Rational Expression and Variables on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be4173d4-2fab-56de-9d24-84bcde3b6c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be4173d4-2fab-56de-9d24-84bcde3b6c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507098} :answer-field/id #uuid "25247a53-b3d9-5d93-a5e2-eb10bd145f04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d3bc34-7b3f-57d7-be3b-ca7e45a1f25b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04d3bc34-7b3f-57d7-be3b-ca7e45a1f25b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506685} :answer-field/id #uuid "754b3a47-c518-5c04-b26c-a2ac39a75809" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "beefe539-fabd-5c70-98d6-47fa9012204c" :question/math-academy-id "q-181384" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $\\frac{2z+9}{3}\\ge -z-1.$\n\nThe solution is $z$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $3:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2z+9}{3} & \\ge -z-1 \\\\ 3\\cdot (\\frac{2z+9}{3}) & \\ge 3\\cdot (-z-1) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2z+9}{\\cancel{3}}) & \\ge 3\\cdot (-z-1) \\\\ 2z+9 & \\ge -3z-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z+9 & \\ge -3z-3 \\\\ 2z+9+3z & \\ge -3z-3+3z \\\\ 5z+9 & \\ge -3 \\\\ 5z+9-9 & \\ge -3-9 \\\\ 5z & \\ge -12 \\\\ \\frac{5z}{5} & \\ge \\frac{-12}{5} \\\\ z & \\ge -\\frac{12}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z\\ge -\\frac{12}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a00ac76c-0ebd-53cb-b689-98bda731064a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing Two Rational Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adfdc82e-f387-5cca-a236-db6c3b237ae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adfdc82e-f387-5cca-a236-db6c3b237ae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507062} :answer-field/id #uuid "909bfc96-ecbc-5d98-91c1-caba1a5f0edc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ced4f854-67c0-55a7-8eb2-2342cefa6036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ced4f854-67c0-55a7-8eb2-2342cefa6036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507128} :answer-field/id #uuid "e46faa19-8528-52c0-9d68-d774c89993c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d5194de3-9348-5e70-86f0-2dc5eae75238" :question/math-academy-id "q-181399" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $\\frac{y+2}{3}<\\frac{y+3}{2}.$\n\nThe solution is $y$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expressions by multiplying both sides of the inequality by the lowest common positive multiple of the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+2}{3} & <\\frac{y+3}{2} \\\\ 6\\cdot (\\frac{y+2}{3}) & <6\\cdot (\\frac{y+3}{2}) \\\\ 2\\cdot (y+2) & <3\\cdot (y+3) \\\\ 2y+4 & <3y+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles. \n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y+4 & <3y+9 \\\\ 2y+4-3y & <3y+9-3y \\\\ 4-y & <9 \\\\ 4-y-4 & <9-4 \\\\ -y & <5 \\\\ \\frac{-y}{-1} & \\,\\,>\\,\\,\\frac{5}{-1} \\\\ y & >-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y>-5.$"}]}
